pySMESH: SMESH_Mesh::AddHypothesis keeps the worst status it found (SMESH V9_16_0; applies
after SMESH_Mesh.patch).

Defect: AddHypothesis checks the sub-shapes of the shape a hypothesis is added to, then the
ancestors of those sub-shapes for concurrent hypotheses, and keeps the worst status of each
check (ret2 > ret). Its last check, CheckHypothesesOnSubMeshes, assigns its result to ret
outright (SMESH_Mesh.cxx:719 at V9_16_0) and so throws away what the checks before it found.

Symptom: two different NumberOfSegments on two faces of a box that share an edge give
HYP_CONCURRENT on the shared edge (SMESH_subMesh::CheckConcurrentHypothesis). AddHypothesis
returns HYP_OK for the second one: the concurrency warning that the status exists for never
reaches the caller. A fatal status found on the sub-shapes is worse: AddHypothesis removes
the hypothesis for it and then returns HYP_OK, so the caller believes it attached.

Root cause: CheckHypothesesOnSubMeshes was added by SMESH 9dd9f7684 (2024-11-08, bos #43370,
"Propagation" on sub-meshes) as `ret = CheckHypothesesOnSubMeshes(...)`, below the two
checks that use `if (ret2 > ret) ret = ret2;`. It returns HYP_OK unless a Propagation
hypothesis on a sub-mesh gives a worse status.

Change, in SMESH_Mesh.cxx only: the result goes to ret2 and is kept only if it is worse,
like the checks above it.

Not changed: what CheckHypothesesOnSubMeshes computes, and every case where it was the worst
status already. The fatal case needs a sub-mesh that refuses the father's algorithm
(HYP_NEED_SHAPE, HYP_NOTCONFORM in SMESH_subMesh::AlgoStateEngine); no combination of the
pySMESH catalogue is known to reach it. pySMESH refuses fatal statuses only, so it refuses
such an assignment now instead of recording it as attached; a HYP_CONCURRENT is returned to
the caller again.
diff --git a/src/SMESH/SMESH_Mesh.cxx b/src/SMESH/SMESH_Mesh.cxx
--- a/src/SMESH/SMESH_Mesh.cxx
+++ b/src/SMESH/SMESH_Mesh.cxx
@@ -722,7 +722,12 @@
       }
     }
 
-    ret = CheckHypothesesOnSubMeshes(subMesh, anHyp, event);
+    // pySMESH: keep the worst status, as the checks above do. A plain assignment here
+    // threw away a fatal status found on the sub-shapes (after anHyp had been removed for
+    // it) and a HYP_CONCURRENT found on the ancestors.
+    ret2 = CheckHypothesesOnSubMeshes(subMesh, anHyp, event);
+    if (ret2 > ret)
+      ret = ret2;
   }
   HasModificationsToDiscard(); // to reset _isModified flag if a mesh becomes empty
   GetMeshDS()->Modified();
